# IMPL-TCC_DB_READER essence pseudocode

<!-- [IMPL-TCC_DB_READER] [ARCH-MACOS_PERM_REPORT] [REQ-MACOS_PERM_REPORT] — readonly TCC database query with partial-report degradation -->

## RESOLVE_TCC_PATHS

```
INPUT: env MAC_PERMS_TCC_USER_DB, MAC_PERMS_TCC_SYSTEM_DB (optional overrides)
OUTPUT: { userPath, systemPath }
EFFECTS: defaults to ~/Library/Application Support/com.apple.TCC/TCC.db and /Library/Application Support/com.apple.TCC/TCC.db
```

## OPEN_TCC_READONLY

```
INPUT: dbPath
OUTPUT: Database handle OR ReadWarning
PRE: path is string
POST: on EACCES/ENOENT return ReadWarning with code DB_UNREADABLE; never throw for expected access denial
EFFECTS: opens SQLite readonly via better-sqlite3
```

## QUERY_BY_SERVICE_AND_STATUS

```
INPUT: db, services[], statusFilter (granted|denied|all)
OUTPUT: TccRow[]
PRE: db is open
POST: rows match service IN services; auth_value filtered by statusFilter
  granted -> auth_value = 2
  denied -> auth_value = 0
  all -> no auth filter
EFFECTS: SELECT service, client, client_type, auth_value, last_modified, indirect_object_identifier FROM access WHERE service IN (?)
```

## MERGE_RESULTS

```
INPUT: userRows[], systemRows[], warnings[]
OUTPUT: { rows: TccRow[], warnings: Warning[] }
POST: dedupe key = (service, client, indirect_object_identifier); later duplicate dropped
```
